<title>UK: Appleton acquitted from price-rig charge.</title>
<headline>Appleton acquitted from price-rig charge.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British paper and packaging group Arjo Wiggins Appleton said on Wednesday that a U.S. court had found its subsidiary and one of its employees not guilty of fixing prices in the U.S. thermal paper market.</p>
<p>Appleton Papers and the employee were indicted by a federal grand jury in Boston in December 1995 for fixing prices during the period between mid-1991 and early 1992.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +0171-542 7717</p>
</text>
